* Sun Sep 27 2026 Johan Hedin - 1.x.y (not released yet)
- Refuse locations in the metadata that are absolute or lead outside of the
  repository, both for directories and URLs
- Refuse redirects from https:// to http:// and to other schemes
- Limit what is downloaded, or read from a compressed file, to the sizes in
  the metadata, and stop following loops in directory listings
- Don't print the password of a proxy URL in error messages
- Print control characters in names from the repository as \xNN
- Warn about packages without checksum with --checksum, and don't stop on a
  package without size in primary.xml
- Always create the TLS context in rrcc, and warn when --insecure is used
- Fix CodeQL findings in the test suite
- Add zsh and fish completions, installed by 'make install' next to the
  bash completion, which has moved to completions/rrcc.bash
- Add --max-age to report repositories whose metadata is older than a
  number of days
- Add --no-strict-x509 to accept certificates that don't follow RFC 5280
  strictly, e.g. from a home-made CA, which Python 3.13+ rejects by default
- Add --quiet to print only the repositories with problems, and nothing
  when all are consistent

* Sat Sep 26 2026 Johan Hedin - 1.4.0
- Add a test suite, run with 'make test' and 'make test-all'
- Reuse the worker threads for all checks of a remote repository
- Add --ignore-modules to use the --newest-only rules of dnf 5, which
  ignores modules, for mirrors made with dnf 5's reposync
- Add GitHub CI workflow
- Add local CI in Podman containers, run with make ci-local

* Sat Sep 26 2026 Johan Hedin - 1.3.0
- Honor the http_proxy, https_proxy and no_proxy environment variables
- Add TLS support for https:// repositories
- Check every metadata file listed in repomd.xml, not just primary

* Sat Sep 26 2026 Johan Hedin - 1.2.1
- Add --newest-only (-n) option to only check the latest packages

* Sat Sep 26 2026 Johan Hedin - 1.2.0
- Add support for checking remote repositories over HTTP(S)

* Sat Sep 26 2026 Johan Hedin - 1.1.1
- Add bash completion
- Add man page

* Sat Sep 26 2026 Johan Hedin - 1.1.0
- Add support for installing on the system using make

* Sat Sep 26 2026 Johan Hedin - 1.0.0
- Initial release
